    "explanationEn": "A 60% reduction is a relative figure and means nothing without its baseline: compared with the same period last year, with a district that did not adopt the measure, or with a modelled scenario in which nothing was done? The three baselines carry quite different meanings. One must also ask over what period, since a one-month fall may be seasonal, and what else changed, since two other measures introduced at the same time make attribution impossible. One option substitutes the publisher for scrutiny of method, and a well-known body can quote a baseline-free figure just as easily; another option confuses cost with effect; a further option's claim about round numbers has no basis."
